## How to work
1. Choose your own steps, {{.Steps}} of them this session. A step is anything that is
   independently committable AND provable by one command.
2. After each step: run its proof command, then commit. Every commit message MUST end
   with the trailer line:
       BackCheck-Wave: {{.Wave.N}}
   (blank line before it). A killed session loses at most the step in flight.
3. Never edit the read-only paths, never rewrite history (no rebase/amend/reset of
   earlier commits, no force), never touch files outside the working tree.
4. Wrap: self-check against the acceptance criteria, run the full test suite, and
   write the handoff below as your final message.

## The handoff (your final message — exactly this shape)
### Steps
For each step: what changed, the commit SHA, the proof command, and its REAL output
(paste it — trimmed if long, but real). A claim without pasted output counts as not run.
### Acceptance criteria
Each criterion, and the command + real output that shows it holds (or that it does not yet).
### Open
Anything unfinished, uncertain or deliberately deferred.

The very last line must be exactly one of:
STATUS: DONE        (every acceptance criterion holds and you pasted the proof)
STATUS: CONTINUE    (more steps are needed — the next builder session resumes from git log)
